Adapted by dishanhai: MuWeapi, selected search/stream/lyric protocol logic from
MuNeteaseApi and MuQQApi (including QR login, QQ OAuth exchange and hash33),
and YRC timing from LyricParser. Player page structure is adapted from NCMScreen,
NavigateBar, ControlsBar, MusicLyricsPanel and AccountManagerOverlay at the same revision.
Modifications: UUK API integration, bounded HTTPS requests, MP3-only sources,
existing SHBUI lyric models and asynchronous session ownership.
These adaptations remain licensed under Apache-2.0, independently of SHBUI's MIT code.
The upstream NOTICE is reproduced unmodified. Selected protocols and page structure are used;
Skija, Skia, platform icons, custom-source scripts and DSP are not distributed here.
QR login adaptations use per-attempt, domain/path-scoped cookies, an exact HTTPS host
allowlist, finite background polling, cancellation and opt-in encrypted credential handoff.
Additional adaptations: account and playlist reads, NetEase liked-song operations and
both providers' search suggestions. QQ liked-song writes use the bounded
QQFavorites request path documented in docs/ONLINE_MUSIC_API.md.
Page adaptations replace the upstream renderer with UUK/native widgets, semantic theme
colors, responsive navigation, search results, a persistent transport bar, contextual
lyrics and account-source cards. No unavailable upstream feature is presented as active.
The separately licensed JavaLayer decoder is documented in ../jlayer/SOURCE.

Additional original presentation: borderless, softly following lyrics, keyboard seek targets,
manual lyric browsing and provider album art. Inspired by MusicLyricsPanel composition;
no QQ Music assets, album images, shaders or fonts are bundled. Album art is fetched
only from the selected music provider at runtime and remains its respective owner's content.

Additional modifications (2026-11-16): music-scoped QQ cookie aliases, strict RPC
status handling, deterministic NetEase playlist pagination, account-library entry
points, retry and stale-request isolation, and confirmed/unknown favorite feedback.
No additional upstream source or third-party assets are bundled by these changes.

Additional modifications (2026-11-17): native session queue inspired by PlayQueuePanel;
all sixteen upstream theme palettes with contrast adjustments for native controls;
shared native page chrome and preference/theme draft history; additional native island
styles and delayed music-capsule hover; spring-following lyric focus and optional
bounded cover-derived fluid background color transitions. These are native adaptations,
not bundled Skija renderers or a complete upstream business/backend distribution.
No additional upstream fonts, branded artwork, or third-party assets are bundled.
